Package: DropoutKiller
Type: Package
Title: Selective Dropout Recovery for Single-Cell RNA Sequencing
Version: 0.8.0
Authors@R: person("DropoutKiller", "Developers", email = "dropoutkiller@users.noreply.github.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Author: DropoutKiller Developers [aut, cre]
Maintainer: DropoutKiller Developers <dropoutkiller@users.noreply.github.com>
Description: Detects recoverable zero events using ALRA evidence, SuperCell
    Walktrap hierarchy neighbor support, and shrunk membership context learned
    by a balanced logistic model. Paired RNA and ATAC Seurat inputs automatically
    rebuild PCA, LSI excluding its first component, and weighted nearest-neighbor
    affinities following the SuperCell 2.0 implementation. Hierarchy borrowing
    is restricted to broad cell classes. A fitted model or explicit artificial
    thinning calibration supplies the detection threshold. Selected zeros are
    recovered with the target-safe cross-fitted P1 stabilized state framework;
    observed nonzero values are preserved on the normalized working scale.
    Historical detectors remain available for explicit comparisons.
